{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQ2taWLzGBunekeKu58w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Palantir's 3-year revenue CAGR is about 22.9%, covering FY2021 to FY2024.**\n\nFY2024 is the latest full fiscal year reported as of 16 May 2025.\n\n| Fiscal year (ending Dec 31) | Revenue |\n|---|---|\n| FY2021 (base year) | $1,541.9M ($1,541,889,000) |\n| FY2022 | $1,905.9M |\n| FY2023 | $2,225.0M |\n| FY2024 (end year) | $2,865.5M ($2,865,507,000) |\n\n**Calculation:** CAGR = (2,865,507,000 ÷ 1,541,889,000)^(1/3) − 1 = (1.8584)^(1/3) − 1 ≈ **22.9%**\n\nRevenue grew about 86% in total over the three years. Growth slowed from 23.6% in 2022 to 16.7% in 2023, then picked up to 28.8% in 2024.\n\nThe revenue figures are the XBRL concept \"Revenue from Contract with Customer, Excluding Assessed Tax.\" The data also includes a 10-K filed in February 2026 with FY2025 figures. That is after the 16 May 2025 cutoff, so I left it out.\n\n**Sources**\n- Form 10-K for FY2024, filed 2025-02-18, accession 0001321655-25-000022 (FY2024, FY2023 and FY2022 revenue)\n- Form 10-K for FY2023, filed 2024-02-20, accession 0001321655-24-000022 (FY2021 revenue, restated comparative)\n- Form 10-K for FY2021, filed 2022-02-24, accession 0001193125-22-050913 (FY2021 revenue as originally reported, same value)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1831,"cache_read_input_tokens":5736,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1831},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6ff6e3b-82f3-4518-876b-395d9cd553a7","uuid":"86ccfc11-3d86-4475-91c2-ecbfd67223ba","timestamp":"2026-10-26T02:08:27.633Z","request_id":"req_011CgQ2taFy4fn1ViKT21GUz"}
